                <pb facs="1079" n="983" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg983"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1898-06-29"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 29,
                    1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>British Government concludes Camara can not remain at Port Said more than
                    twenty-four hours, except in case of necessity, and can not coal there if he has
                    coal enough to take him back to Cadiz, which appears to be the case.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hay.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
